WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.913 --> 00:00:02.341
- Jeremy is a garden snail.

00:00:02.341 --> 00:00:04.866
At first glance, he looks
like any other snail.

00:00:04.866 --> 00:00:06.497
A bit small, perhaps.

00:00:06.497 --> 00:00:09.145
And one of his tentacles
is slightly askew.

00:00:09.145 --> 00:00:11.585
But there's actually something
remarkable about Jeremy

00:00:11.585 --> 00:00:13.908
that makes him different from the rest.

00:00:13.908 --> 00:00:16.241
His shell coils to the left.

00:00:20.223 --> 00:00:23.486
Jeremy was discovered by a
compost heap in southwest London.

00:00:23.486 --> 00:00:26.499
A retired scientist spotted
the extraordinary mollusk

00:00:26.499 --> 00:00:28.336
and made a phone call to this man.

00:00:28.336 --> 00:00:30.256
Well, this man being me.

00:00:30.256 --> 00:00:31.089
Hi, there.

00:00:31.089 --> 00:00:32.073
I'm Dr. Angus Davison.

00:00:32.073 --> 00:00:34.473
I've been researching
snails now for 20 years

00:00:34.473 --> 00:00:36.644
and Jeremy might be the most unusual snail

00:00:36.644 --> 00:00:39.132
I've ever encountered.

00:00:39.132 --> 00:00:41.209
Most snail shells coil to the right.

00:00:41.209 --> 00:00:43.370
Jeremy's left-coiling
shell is exciting for us

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.161
because it's extremely rare.

00:00:45.161 --> 00:00:46.631
It's an opportunity to research

00:00:46.631 --> 00:00:48.828
whether or not he can
pass his unique traits

00:00:48.828 --> 00:00:50.257
on to his offspring.

00:00:50.257 --> 00:00:51.968
Eventually, we may even be able to

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:54.534
apply our learnings to human beings.

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:56.162
But, in order to maximize the research,

00:00:56.162 --> 00:00:57.959
we need Jeremy to reproduce.

00:00:57.959 --> 00:01:01.259
Unfortunately, he's not
the most seductive suitor.

00:01:01.259 --> 00:01:02.731
Typically, a snail's sex organs

00:01:02.731 --> 00:01:04.764
are on the right side of their head.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:07.697
But, with Jeremy, his
genitals are on the left.

00:01:07.697 --> 00:01:11.530
This little mix-up makes
things a bit awkward.

00:01:12.555 --> 00:01:15.204
We tried pairing Jeremy
with a few righties,

00:01:15.204 --> 00:01:16.346
but I had no luck.

00:01:16.346 --> 00:01:18.422
So, I went on the radio
to make a casting call.

00:01:18.422 --> 00:01:20.090
So, if you are really lucky

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:23.312
and you find one of these
very rare left-coiling snails,

00:01:23.312 --> 00:01:24.941
I'd love to hear from you.

00:01:24.941 --> 00:01:26.653
I was pessimistic at first.

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:29.503
Snails like Jeremy are one in 100,000.

00:01:29.503 --> 00:01:32.071
But, within a few days,
the phone started ringing.

00:01:32.071 --> 00:01:33.581
(phone ringing)

00:01:33.581 --> 00:01:36.688
- Hi, I'm Jade Melton
in Ipswich, Suffolk,

00:01:36.688 --> 00:01:39.620
a snail enthusiast with over 300 snails.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.373
And this one, Leftie,

00:01:41.373 --> 00:01:44.513
might make the perfect match for Jeremy.

00:01:44.513 --> 00:01:47.325
Leftie and Jeremy both
have left-coiling shells

00:01:47.325 --> 00:01:50.054
and genitals on the left side.

00:01:50.054 --> 00:01:51.443
Right now, the two are resting,

00:01:51.443 --> 00:01:53.114
but, once their energies are high enough,

00:01:53.114 --> 00:01:55.398
we hope they'll mate
and produce some eggs.

00:01:55.398 --> 00:01:56.539
- We are looking for a connection

00:01:56.539 --> 00:01:58.657
between the snails and their eggs.

00:01:58.657 --> 00:02:00.004
A discovery could teach us something

00:02:00.004 --> 00:02:01.756
about our own genetics.

00:02:01.756 --> 00:02:04.772
And, if not, at least Jeremy,
the left-coiled snail,

00:02:04.772 --> 00:02:06.688
was able to find love.

00:02:06.688 --> 00:02:09.855
And that's got to count for something.

